{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:700a0453398913da","name":"Rapid Strike","source":{"id":"source:reference-700a0453398913da","title":"Rapid Strike","revision":24955,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T16:07:10Z","sha256":"01e1d78554b48a8a2629d7dd0a6acd8230eafc2a0a90c0c2176eb4fc0cc51031","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24955","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Rapid%20Strike&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-700a0453398913da","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["You make two quick strikes with a melee weapon as a single attack.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," +1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Effect:"]}," When using a melee weapon with which you are proficient, you may make two strikes as a single attack against a single target. You take a -2 penalty on your attack roll, but deal +1 die of damage with a successful attack.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," The effects of this feat do not stack with the extra damage provided by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mighty Swing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mighty_Swing","referenceId":"reference:9f931d147940b545"}," feat. If you do not have a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," score of 13 or higher, increase the penalty to attacks to -5 when using this feat with non-",{"tag":"a","children":["Light Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Light_Weapons"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," I think the prerequisites for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Shot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Shot","referenceId":"reference:d5cac053fa8ba463"}," and Rapid Strike were swapped accidentally. Wouldn't it make more sense for Rapid Strike, a melee ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"},", to have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," requirement, and for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Shot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Shot","referenceId":"reference:d5cac053fa8ba463"},", a ranged ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"},", to have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," requirement?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," No, this is intentional. For ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Shot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Shot","referenceId":"reference:d5cac053fa8ba463"},", you need the higher ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," to control the recoil of firing multiple shots so quickly. For Rapid Strike, you need the higher ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," to have the agility necessary to get two swings for the price of one- catching your target a second time on the backswing, spinning to come around a second time, and so on.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For balance purposes, this also has the effect of giving characters some tough decisions. A ranged specialist won't always want to neglect their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"},", and a melee specialist won't want to neglect their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"},". (Sure, such a character could neglect ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," if they have ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Finesse"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Finesse","referenceId":"reference:7752dd7b768faff2"},", but they're spending an extra ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"}," and restricting themselves to certain weapons for that privilege.)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Rapid Strike and Whirlwind Attack"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," Reading the rules, it seems that you can use Rapid Strike in conjunction with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Whirlwind Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Whirlwind_Attack","referenceId":"reference:42e4a091048fa93e"},", gaining an extra die of damage against all targets. Is this correct?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," No, they don't work together, nor will ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Shot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Shot","referenceId":"reference:d5cac053fa8ba463"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Autofire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Autofire"},". The text of both Rapid Strike and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Shot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Shot","referenceId":"reference:d5cac053fa8ba463"}," mention that they work with a single attack roll against a single target. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attacks"}," (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Whirlwind Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Whirlwind_Attack","referenceId":"reference:42e4a091048fa93e"},") deal with multiple targets, so they are not eligible.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
